  <h2>Community information</h2>
  <p>Love Mallacoota provides a free directory and community information service. Listings, dates, opening hours, links and contact details can change. Confirm time-sensitive or important details directly with the relevant business, organisation or authority.</p>
  <h2>No endorsement</h2>
  <p>Listing a business, event, group or external link does not mean we endorse it. Sponsored material is identified separately from community content.</p>
  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not misuse the site, attempt to disrupt it, submit unlawful material, impersonate another person or knowingly provide false information.</p>
  <h2>Rights and reuse</h2>
  <p>Original platform content is released under Creative Commons BY 4.0. Community-supplied and third-party material remains subject to its owner’s rights. Code is MIT licensed. Full terms are in <a href="https://github.com/coldix/lovemallacoota/blob/main/CONTENT-LICENCE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CONTENT-LICENCE.md</a> in the project repository.</p>
  <h2>Weather, tides and other information</h2>
  <p>The forecast and the sea level shown here come from an open weather model. They are indicative and are <strong>not for navigation</strong>: the heights are modelled against mean sea level rather than chart datum, at a point offshore rather than at the inlet entrance, and take no account of wind or barometric pressure. Use the Bureau of Meteorology or another official source before crossing the bar or going out. Nothing here is an emergency service — see <a href="/emergency.html">emergency information</a>.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>Advertising is labelled. We accept political advertising, which must carry the authorisation Australian law requires; carrying an advertisement is not an endorsement of it. See the <a href="/editorial-policy.html">editorial policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>What you keep when you contribute</h2>
  <p>You keep the copyright in what you write and photograph. By submitting, you give us permission to publish it here, in the weekly edition, in the printable edition and in the archive of past editions, and you confirm it is yours to give — that you took the photograph or have the photographer's agreement, and that anyone identifiable in it is content to appear.</p>
  <p>Published material forms part of a public record stored in a public repository. You can ask us to take something down and we will; see <a href="/privacy.html">privacy</a> for what that can and cannot undo.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>These terms may be updated as the platform develops. Material changes will be dated and recorded in the public project history.</p>
